                                "sense_id": "56905439-eae5-31b5-ac47-3285e486dbe0",
                                "text": "Lennard knew well every nook, crevice, and shelf of the quarry; on many a day in boyhood he had birdnested among the gorse that fringed its mouth, or fished for minnows and \"pow-wowets\" with a luggie and string in the slimy pool at the bottom; […]"
